[%think 106589] [%out 107125] [%in 2] [%cacheread 0] [%cachewrite 1987] Red is
a full rook up, so the aim is to activate the remaining pieces and create
threats rather than grab more. **What Black threatens:** - Red's e3 pawn is
attacked twice, by the knight on d5 and the cannon on e7 (through e6), and
defended only once, by the knight on g2. With accurate play Black can win this
pawn whatever Red does. Even Rb3 runs into …炮8退4 (h7h3), which adds a third
attacker via g3. - …马4进6 (d5f4) would attack the unprotected red knight on
g2. **Why 车一进一 (i0i1):** 1. It develops the last idle rook and threatens
车一平四 (Rf1+) down the open f-file. - If Black answers with the king to e9,
马七进七 (a9c8) is mate. The knight covers e9 through the empty d8, f9 is
controlled by the rook, and nothing can block d8 or take the knight. - So Black
would have to block with a piece, and Ae8-f7 weakens the palace. 2. If Black
plays …马4进6 (d5f4), 车一平四 (Rf1) pins that knight to the king. It cannot
move and nothing defends it, so it is lost. 3. If Black takes on e3 with the
knight, 马三进五 (Nxe3) and then …炮xe3 follows. Now Rf1+ comes with tempo, and
车八进三 (Rb3) can chase the cannon. Red is still up a rook for a pawn and has
the initiative. 4. The rook on the first rank also guards d1 and f1 against
later knight raids. } 将６平５ 13. 车一平四 { [%emt 0:10:37] [%think 64683]
